---
title: Lentil & Tomato Pie
author: Shirley Simmonds
servings: 4
cook time: 40 minutes
---

Peel and chop @onion{1}(large) and fry it in @butter{5%g} or @margarine{} in a #saucepan{} until it's golden and beginning to soften, about ~{5-6%minutes}, then add @lentils{175%g}(split red, washed) and @garlic{1}(crushed) and stir for a moment or two before adding @stock or @water{500%ml}.

Bring the mixture up to the boil, half-cover with a lid and simmer for about ~{20%minutes}, until the lentils are soft and pale golden.

Remove the saucepan from the heat and add @tomatoes{}(skinned and chopped), @cheese{75%g}(grated), @basil{1%tsp}(dried), @lemon juice{1%tbsp}, @egg{1} and @salt{} and @black pepper{}(freshly ground) to taste. Leave the mixture to cool.

Roll out about two-thirds of @pastry{275%g}(shortcrust) and use to line an 8 inch (20 cm) flan dish or sandwich tin. Roll the remainder into a circle to fit the top of the dish.

Preheat the oven to 200°C. Spread the lentil mixture into the pastry case. Dampen the edges of the pastry with a little cold water, then put the circle of pastry on top and press down lightly, crimping the edges.

Prick the top and brush with a little @beaten egg{} if you want a shiny finish. Bake the pie in the preheated oven for about ~{40%minutes}, until the pastry is golden brown and crisp.
